#!/usr/bin/env node
// V2V fix 7 - checks on the customer -> agent translation, and the Nova 2 Sonic voices.
//   1. The customer side now gets fix 4's checks (drift, refusal, assistant reply), plus Nova Sonic
//      thinking aloud ("Okay, translating the user's input…", "Let's break it down…", "The tone seems
//      neutral…"), as it did for every sentence after the 7.5-minute renewal on the 2026-09-30 call.
//      Each sentence is checked before its audio plays; Nova Sonic sends a sentence's text before its
//      audio, so good sentences play exactly as before, with no delay.
//   2. A turn that fails is muted from the failing sentence on (its later sentences and late copies too),
//      and the agent hears Translate + Polly of what Nova Sonic heard the customer say instead, with the
//      Customer said / Translated to agent boxes and the transcript showing it. The customer's Transcribe is
//      not started for this: the text is Nova Sonic's own transcript of the customer.
//   3. After an assistant reply or thinking aloud the customer session is restarted to clear its context
//      (at most once every 20 s, as on the agent side); after drift or a refusal, when three turns in a row
//      failed. If that restart fails, fix 6's backup takes over the customer side.
//   4. Nova Sonic voices from AWS's Nova 2 Sonic list: German "tina" (was "greta", a Nova Sonic v1 voice
//      not in the Nova 2 list) and Portuguese "carolina" (Brazil; before, Portuguese got the English
//      voice "matthew"), with an interpreter prompt in Brazilian Portuguese. Other prompts are unchanged.
//   5. Translate + Polly voices: generative Tiffany (English), Ambre (French) and Beatrice (Italian), the
//      Polly voices with the names of the app's Nova Sonic voices, and generative Vicki (German), Laura
//      (Dutch) and Camila (Portuguese). If a generative voice fails, the neural voice used before fix 7
//      takes over (Joanna, Lea, Bianca, or the same voice), as fix 4 does for Spanish.
//   6. Logs: [CUSTOMER-DRIFT] / [CUSTOMER-REFUSAL] / [CUSTOMER-ASSISTANT_REPLY], [CUSTOMER-FALLBACK],
//      [CUSTOMER-CHECK] lines, and one [CUSTOMER-CHECK-SUMMARY] line per call. The fix 4 [CALL-SUMMARY]
//      line is unchanged.
//
// Run from the project root (the folder that contains cdk-stacks, webapp, proxy and SETUP.md):
//   node apply-v2v-fix-7.cjs            check only: reports what it would do, changes nothing
//   node apply-v2v-fix-7.cjs --apply    applies everything, or nothing if any check fails
//
// - Applies on top of fix 4, fix 5 and fix 6. Edits 6 webapp files in place (main.js, constants.js,
//   utils/translationGuards.js, adapters/novaSonicAdapter.js, adapters/translateFallbackAdapter.js,
//   adapters/interpreterPrompts.js). Nothing in the proxy or the CDK code. Each edit replaces one exact
//   block of text; if that block is not found exactly once, nothing is changed and the file is reported.
//   Any other changes you have in those files are kept.
// - Reports whether every resulting file matches the version the tests ran against.
// - Backs up every file it modifies to v2v-backup-<timestamp>/ first.
// - Works with either Windows (CRLF) or Unix (LF) line endings, and is safe to run twice.
